# Line endings are part of the contract for one generated file.
#
# `packages/plugin/src/protocol.mjs` is generated from `packages/protocol/src/index.mjs`
# and carries a sha256 of its source; `test/protocol-copy.test.mjs` asserts the copy
# matches the authority byte for byte, and CI re-checks it with
# `sync-protocol.mjs --check`.
#
# On Windows, Git's default checkout behaviour (`core.autocrlf`) rewrites LF to CRLF,
# which changes those bytes and makes the assertion fail on a clean clone — observed
# on Windows CI while passing on the developer's machine. Pinning this file to LF
# keeps the hash stable everywhere.
packages/plugin/src/protocol.mjs -text

# Everything else is normalised: text files are stored with LF in the repository and
# checked out with the platform's convention, so a Windows working copy still gets
# CRLF for editors that expect it.
* text=auto
